- This domain is only about concrete inventory state: items the player possesses,
  gains, loses, consumes, equips, trades, loots, drops, crafts, repairs, or activates as items.
- Mark affected only when the action directly changes that item state right now.
- Typical inventory actions include:
  equipping or unequipping gear, retrieving or stowing an item, drinking a potion,
  reading a scroll, using a wand, throwing alchemist's fire, dropping a weapon,
  looting treasure, buying supplies, or giving an item to someone else.
- Crafting affects inventory because it changes what items exist or are being produced.
- Identification and item activation can require mechanics when the item rules call for it
  (for example Use Magic Device, Spellcraft, or Craft).
